- Story & Context: During a live alignment session, one glass bowl begins drifting sharp as the room temperature rises. The sequencer remains locked, but the acoustic beating against the veena grows faster and increasingly uncomfortable. Marcus initially tries to compensate with oscillator tuning. Ananya stops him and instead shifts her drone string slightly, causing the entire harmonic center to move by a small but audible amount. Karthik responds by abandoning the established percussion phrase and introducing a three-stroke cadence that resolves against the new tuning. The audience hears the ensemble reorganize in real time. No one stops the track. The apparent technical error becomes the formal turning point: bass sequence drops out, dry kick continues alone, glass harmonica and veena negotiate the unstable interval, then the rhythm section re-enters around the new center. The final cadence deliberately avoids retuning to the original reference. The performance ends on the altered pitch, documenting the fact that an acoustic system changed and the machines had to follow.
